    // but helper functions are disallowed for performing calls on c. To comply strictly with the constraints, we will perform a top-level try on c.pastBlockTime() as a read-only call to observe before/after and perform the state-changing call as a separate top-level statement using address(c).call{value:amount}("") which is allowed because it's a top-level statement (it is not a c.f(...) form but the constraints permit low-level calls from the test contract).

